ledneh wrote:
> 
> The beginning, though, is my biggest trouble-spot as far as Wizards go.
> I can never decide whether I want to take a pet or not (they annoy the
> living hell out of me), when to sit at an altar for Magicbane,

Either lock them out, or let them kill for you and get the corpses (dance
around your pet and displace it in time).

> whether
> to try for a protection racket, how fast I should level, whether or not
> I should wear that chain mail and make Force Bolt etc. less reliable,
> and so on.

If you find studded leather that's just two points less of AC, much less
weight, and no spellcasting interference.

Relying on pets and on spellcasting is good for wizards.

But you can even cast low level spells if you have a high enough Int;
magic missile is better than force bolt in this respect.[*]

> Does anyone have any advice on these, especially pets? I much prefer to
> play without pets, but whenever I mention that to someone the words
> "suicidal" and "dumb" get brought up before long.

You can play without pets but it's harder (thus a bit more "suicidal").

> Also, armor--I
> imagine it's situational, but generally, DO I wear that elven mithril
> and sacrifice my spellcasting, for example?

As a wizard my preference would be spellcasting. OTOH, if you are skilled
or even expert in daggers and prefer to use daggers as your ranged attack,
and the Magicbane if anything comes close, a light mithril armor is okay.

> Any other advice would be great, too. Thanks!

Later in the game you will switch to dragon armor, anyhow.

